=== PARITY (vs web TelemetryErrorsWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (TelemetryErrorsSource ->
    TelemetryErrorsModel): useFleetTelemetryErrorVINs, useFleetTelemetryErrors,
    useTelemetry(seam), useTranslation. The production app wires TelemetryErrorsSource over the
    KMP TelemetryStore (two StateHolderModel<LoadableState<…>> coalesced) polling
    /tesla/fleet-telemetry/error-vins + /tesla/fleet-telemetry/errors on STALE_TIMES.STANDARD.
    The view performs NO HTTP — no direct transport in the view (ADR-002/009).
  Projection -> TelemetryErrorsProjection.aggregate is a 1:1 port of the web `aggregated` useMemo:
    group by vin + (error_code ?? raw 'unknown') key; sum count; track latest (reported_at ??
    fetched_at); display code falls back to localized "Unknown"; sort newest-first with undated
    rows last, STABLE on ties (matches the web Map insertion order under a stable sort).
    activeVINCount = Σ active; hasData = vins||errors; isRecent = now-lastSeen < 1h (ONE_HOUR_MS).
    Verified by EXECUTED XCTest (testAggregate*, testActiveVINCount*, testIsRecent*).
  States (every one renders — no hidden surfaces):
    loading  -> skeleton chrome (feed skeletons / compact skeleton)            [web WidgetShell loading]
    empty    -> ContentUnavailableView "No telemetry error data"               [web !hasData EmptyState]
    error    -> QueryError-equivalent (icon + title + message + Retry)         [prompt-required + web isError]
    content  -> compact (count + "error VINs" + status badge) OR standard
                (active-VIN header + status badge + scrollable error feed;
                 inner "No errors recorded" when aggregated is empty)          [web isCompact / standard]
    freshness chip (header) maps the web DataFreshness states:
      live(fresh)/fetching("updating…")/stale/error("error")/offline          [web DataFreshness]
      — tappable to refresh (web onClick onRefresh); compact = title-less (web compact).
  i18n -> every web key resolves through the P1/S10 facade (TelemetryErrorsStrings, table
    "TelemetryErrorsWidget"); NO English literal in code. Source keys present:
      widget.telemetryErrors.title / .unknown / .errors / .healthy / .noData / .errorVINs /
      .activeVINs ("%lld VINs with errors") / .noErrors / .recent  (9/9)
    + registry .description + native chrome (.offline/.updating/.errorChip/.refresh/.retry/
      widget.open/.loading/.errorTitle/.emptyHint) + relative buckets (.justNow/.minAgo/.hourAgo/
      .dayAgo) + a11y (.countA11y/.openA11y).
  Registry -> canonical registry/system.ts "telemetry-errors": category=system,
    default 2×4, min 1×2, max 4×40; clamp() enforces the envelope. Verified by XCTest.
  A11y -> VoiceOver labels on every interactive element (freshness/refresh chip, open button,
    Retry) + combined status/count summary + per-row label (VIN/code/×count/relative/recent);
